      "content": "everything just feels so noisy and heavy lately. like i'm just performing this endless, meaningless script every day. if the universe is just cold, empty math, then why is there this massive pressure to keep existing? it feels like we're just being forced to endure a cosmic joke that isn't even funny. wouldn't it be more rational to just opt out of the equation entirely once you realize the sum is always zero?",
